WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:11.400
<v Priya Raman>Okay, we're recording. The main thing today is the Aventra renewal, because their current term ends on the thirty-first and we still don't have a signature.</v>

2
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:19.800
<v Priya Raman>Marcus, you've been closest to it. Where did we land after Thursday's call?</v>

3
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:34.200
<v Marcus Bell>So they came back with a counter. They want the same seat count but at the old rate, which is about twelve percent below what we quoted. Their argument is that they've had three outages this quarter.</v>

4
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:41.600
<v Marcus Bell>I told them I'd take it back to the team but that I couldn't commit to anything on the call.</v>

5
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:47.900
<v Dana Okafor>Three outages is right, but two of those were the upstream provider, not us.</v>

6
00:00:47.900 --> 00:01:02.300
<v Dana Okafor>We have the incident reports. If we're going to give ground on price I'd rather we do it because we want to keep the logo, not because we've accepted a version of events that isn't accurate.</v>

7
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:08.100
<v Priya Raman>That's fair. Marcus, did they put the outage argument in writing anywhere?</v>

8
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:14.700
<v Marcus Bell>It's in the email thread from the fourteenth. I can forward it after this.</v>

9
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:29.500
<v Priya Raman>Please do. Here's where I land: I'm willing to go to six percent, not twelve, and I want the incident report attached to the counter so the number is clearly a goodwill gesture and not an admission.</v>

10
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:35.200
<v Dana Okafor>I can have the report cleaned up and shareable by tomorrow afternoon.</v>

11
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:44.800
<v Marcus Bell>Then I'll send the revised terms Thursday morning. If they push past six I'll bring it back rather than deciding on the call.</v>

12
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.300
<v Priya Raman>Agreed. Let's not go past six without talking first.</v>
